 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Decorator:** `@needs_app_scope`, defined at `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It wraps a callback so it runs inside the app context.\n\n- If you register the command with `@app.cli.command()` or `@bundle.cli.command()`, you don't need it. `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:413`) applies it for you. `app.cli` is an `AppGroup`, created at `src/tessel/app.py:338`.\n- Use `@needs_app_scope` explicitly only for a plain `@click.command()`.\n- To opt out of the wrapping, pass `needs_app_scope=False` to `.command()`.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` in `src/tessel/cli.py:293`, through `LaunchInfo.load_app()` at line 333. The decorator calls `ctx.ensure_object(LaunchInfo).load_app()` and then enters `app.app_context()`.\n\n`TesselGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:531`) is the top-level CLI group. It subclasses `AppGroup` and isn't the thing that loads the app.",
